<article class="env-example" id="043O">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/043O">Example <span data-tag="043O">78.7.6</span> <span class="named">(Constant group algebraic space)</span>.</a>  Let $B \to S$ as in Section <a href="/tag/043A" data-tag="043A">78.3</a>. Let $G$ be an abstract group. Consider the functor which associates to any scheme $T$ over $B$ the group of locally constant maps $T \to G$ (where $T$ has the Zariski topology and $G$ the discrete topology). This is representable by the group algebraic space </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  G_ B = B \times _ S G_ S  \]
</div>
  <p> over $B$. Here $G_ S$ is the constant group scheme introduced in Groupoids, Example <a href="/tag/03YW" data-tag="03YW">39.5.6</a>. </p>
</article>